thread_12_summary:Thread 12 = OPEN_POSITIVE_TARGETS.md §P12 — succinct VERIFICATION of pi(x): an untrusted prover who did the Theta~(x)-or-worse work convinces a verifier of the exact value of pi(x) (or a pi-adjacent count) at sublinear verifier cost. Two soundness regimes: (a) UNCONDITIONAL (interactive sum-check/GKR, information-theoretic soundness) — the project-preferred regime; (b) computational (Fiat-Shamir/SNARK, succinct non-interactive certificate). This is the first thread in 491 sessions to attack the VERIFICATION complexity of pi(x) rather than its computation complexity. The S18+S48 sumcheck closures attacked the truth-table-MLE layer with the computation goal (verifier must evaluate dense MLE of chi_P, prover must be polylog); both objections dissolve in the verification frame: the prover is ALLOWED Theta~(x) work, and the verifier evaluates MLEs of structured sieve predicates (automaton class) or GKR-arithmetized circuits, never the dense chi_P table. S491 PoC (experiments/constructions/p12_sumcheck_pi_verification/) already demonstrates: unconditionally-sound sum-check verification of partial-sieve counts Phi(2^n, P) with verifier O(n*sum p) field ops, exact count match at n=20, 100/100 adaptive cheating provers rejected, <1KB communication. KNOWN GAP defining the thread: full pi(x) needs wheel primes <= sqrt(x), making the naive verifier final-check O~(x/log x); slots 2-3 attack this gap (layered GKR product-tree; native protocol for Meissel-Lehmer/Lucy_Hedgehog DP). Cross-domain import: verifiable computation / doubly-efficient interactive proofs (LFKN 1992, GKR 2008, CMT 2012, Thaler PAZK book) — a field the project has never used beyond the two mis-scoped S18/S48 rows.
thread_12_a_grade_targets:(a) working protocol verifying EXACT pi(x) at concrete x with verifier cost asymptotically and wall-clock below recomputation at matched (unconditional) soundness — criterion (b)+(d) partial-positive, the verification analogue of S224; (b) native sum-check protocol for the Meissel-Lehmer phi(x,a)/Lucy_Hedgehog DP with unconditional verifier O~(sqrt(x)) or better — new structural fact about the DP (not a literature corollary); (c) the automaton-MLE classification theorem: exact characterization of which sieve predicates admit O(n*W) low-degree-extension evaluation, with the primality indicator provably outside (ties to E2.1) — new edge.
thread_12_slot_plan:
  slot_1: harden + scale the S491 PoC. Larger n (24-32 via streamed prover), bigger wheels (primes <= 100), q~2^61 or extension field; adversarial battery (structured cheats: wrong single round, wrong final claim, colluding rounds); measure verifier scaling law empirically; write the automaton-MLE primitive as a clean reusable module; state the polylog-wheel theorem precisely (unconditional IP for Phi(x, polylog-wheel) with polylog verifier).
  slot_2: attack the full-wheel gap, route A — layered arithmetization. Express Phi(x, P_sqrt(x)) as a log-depth product tree / OR-tree over (d, q) witnesses of compositeness and run GKR-style layer reduction; the open question is whether the wiring/input MLEs stay verifier-evaluable in o(x/log x). Honest fallback: quantify the exact verifier exponent achievable by route A.
  slot_3: attack the full-wheel gap, route B — native protocol for the counting DP. Prover commits to Lucy_Hedgehog/Meissel-Lehmer intermediate-state claims (the O(sqrt(x)) distinct floor-values table); design sum-check consistency tests over the recursion. Target: unconditional verifier O~(sqrt(x)) for exact pi(x). This is the genuinely-new-math slot; failure mode (DP transitions lack low-degree structure) is itself a B-grade structural edge.
  slot_4: benchmark + soundness-regime comparison. Verify exact pi(x) at the largest reachable x; wall-clock verifier-vs-recomputation crossover (sympy primepi / Lucy DP / primesieve as baselines); compare unconditional-interactive vs Fiat-Shamir-noninteractive costs; characterize when verification beats independent recomputation as the trust mechanism for published pi(x) records.
  slot_5: theoretical wrap. The verification-complexity landscape theorem for pi(x): (i) polylog verifier with computational soundness via GKR-over-primality-circuit (precise statement of the literature corollary with uniformity conditions); (ii) best unconditional verifier exponent from slots 2-3; (iii) lower-bound discussion (information-theoretic edges of the project applied to the verifier's view); EDGES.md entries; CLOSED_PATHS scope-correction rows finalized; successor proposals.
